                    <p
style="font-size:13px;color:#555555;
                        font-style:italic;margin-top:0;"> September
                      details remain tentative; launch details will be
                      sent on the FoxHunting list. The finish location
                      is intentionally undisclosed and must be found
                      during the hunt. </p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> About
                      the Events </h3>
                    <p> <strong>August</strong> is an on-foot ARDF hunt
                      using a low-power (milliwatt) hidden transmitter,
                      the “fox.” Participants use directional antennas
                      and signal-strength techniques to locate it on
                      foot through the park. These are great events for
                      newcomers — no prior experience is needed. </p>
                    <p> <strong>September</strong> steps up to a full
                      regional mobile T-hunt in west Snohomish County.
                      You will take signal bearings while driving south
                      of Marysville and west of SR-9, then complete a
                      short on-foot leg to the finish location, which is
                      intentionally undisclosed. </p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> What
                      Is Fox Hunting? </h3>
                    <p> Amateur Radio Direction Finding (ARDF) is a
                      radio sport where participants use a directional
                      antenna to locate a hidden transmitter. It
                      combines RF skills, outdoor navigation, and
                      teamwork. Any license class can participate.</p>
                    <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:24px 0 8px;"> How to
                      Get Involved </h3>
                    <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Show up
                          and hunt</strong> — mentors will be present at
                        every event, all skill levels are welcome. </li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Borrow
                          gear</strong> — handheld transceivers and
                        tape-measure Yagi antennas available at each
                        event; no equipment required to attend. </li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Fill out
                          the interest survey</strong> — lets us plan
                        loaner gear and mentoring: <a
                          href="https://forms.gle/LMkWH3sisKHKjaAJ9"
                          style="color:#1a3a5c;">
                          forms.gle/LMkWH3sisKHKjaAJ9 </a> </li>
                      <li style="margin-bottom:8px;"> <strong>Spread
                          the word</strong> — invite a friend; new faces
                        are always welcome. </li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Check in with net control on the K7LED repeater
                      at 146.82Mhz, with a standard negative offset and
                      a PL tone of 103.5Hz, at hunt start (or when you
                      begin hunting). </p>
                    <p>RSVP to <a
                        href="mailto:FoxHunting@mkarc.groups.io"
                        class="moz-txt-link-freetext">FoxHunting@mkarc.groups.io</a>
                      is requested, not required. Questions? Contact <strong>Tom
                        Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at <a
                        href="mailto:TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com"
                        class="moz-txt-link-freetext">TSayles@Soot-n-Smoke.com</a>,
                      or reply to this message. Limited loaner equipment
                      (handheld radio and tape-measure Yagi antenna)
                      will be available by request. Or you can contact
                      Tom and he'll get you a kit and help you make your
                      own antenna. </p>
                    <p> More information at <a
                        href="https://mikeandkey.org/foxhunt.php"
                        style="color:#1a3a5c;">
                        mikeandkey.org/foxhunt.php </a>. </p>
